<figure class="scenario-matrix not-prose my-10 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-card)]">
  <header class="border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--accent)]">Scenario outcomes</p>
      <span class="font-editorial-mono rounded-full border border-[var(--border-subtle)] px-2.5 py-1 text-[8px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Same truth · different evidence</span>
    </div>
    <h3 class="font-display mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-2xl">What changes, what the UI may do, and where it must stop.</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">The scenarios differ because the available evidence changes—not because the interface is allowed to guess.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="scenario-header hidden md:grid" aria-hidden="true">
    <span>Scenario</span>
    <span>What changes</span>
    <span>UI may do</span>
    <span>Boundary</span>
  </div>

  <ol class="scenario-rows" aria-label="Phase 1 scenario outcomes">
    <li class="scenario-row">
      <div class="scenario-cell scenario-name">
        <span class="mobile-label">Scenario</span>
        <span class="row-number">01</span>
        <strong>Several compatible connections</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">What changes</span>
        <p>Data Connection is missing and several compatible options remain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell allowed-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">UI may do</span>
        <p>Explain the requirement, highlight or focus the field, and provide selection guidance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell boundary-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">Boundary</span>
        <p>Do not choose a connection. The application does not know the user’s intent.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="scenario-row">
      <div class="scenario-cell scenario-name">
        <span class="mobile-label">Scenario</span>
        <span class="row-number">02</span>
        <strong>Exactly one compatible connection</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">What changes</span>
        <p>Only one compatible Data Connection remains.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell allowed-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">UI may do</span>
        <p>State that it is the only compatible option and offer an explicit <strong>Use [connection]</strong> action.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell boundary-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">Boundary</span>
        <p>Do not silently mutate configuration. The user accepts the preconfiguration.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="scenario-row">
      <div class="scenario-cell scenario-name">
        <span class="mobile-label">Scenario</span>
        <span class="row-number">03</span>
        <strong>New versus experienced users</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">What changes</span>
        <p>User familiarity changes while application truth does not.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell allowed-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">UI may do</span>
        <p>Show authored conceptual explanation to a new user and omit that beginner fragment for an experienced user.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell boundary-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">Boundary</span>
        <p>The underlying validation rule remains identical.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="scenario-row">
      <div class="scenario-cell scenario-name">
        <span class="mobile-label">Scenario</span>
        <span class="row-number">04</span>
        <strong>Version 4.1 versus 4.2</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">What changes</span>
        <p>The product version changes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell allowed-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">UI may do</span>
        <p>Surface the version 4.2 release-note fragment only for 4.2.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell boundary-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">Boundary</span>
        <p>Version context changes the explanation, not whether the current state is valid.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="scenario-row">
      <div class="scenario-cell scenario-name">
        <span class="mobile-label">Scenario</span>
        <span class="row-number">05</span>
        <strong>Valid selection</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">What changes</span>
        <p>A valid Data Connection has been selected.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell allowed-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">UI may do</span>
        <p>Remove the missing-connection intervention as the state becomes valid.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-cell boundary-cell">
        <span class="mobile-label">Boundary</span>
        <p>Do not keep surfacing warnings or suggestions merely because related knowledge exists.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <figcaption class="flex flex-col gap-2 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)] px-5 py-3 text-[10px] text-[var(--text-muted)] sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between sm:px-6">
    <span>More evidence can justify more help.</span>
    <span class="font-editorial-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--accent)]">Ambiguity still limits authority</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

